#====================================================================
# E227 — Unified patch context prefixes versus outer Git whitespace checks
# 知识草稿，拟对应文档: drafts/E227-draft-0EB3.md
#
# 格式规则:
#   - key: value（冒号后一个空格，value 到行尾）
#   - 多行值: 下一行以空格开头 = 续行
#   - 列表值: 逗号分隔
#   - 正则值: | 分隔多个模式
#   - 以 # 开头的行为注释
#   - 空行忽略
#====================================================================

# ═══ Layer 0: 错误面 (Error Surface) ═══
# trigger_tool: 出错的工具 (configure/cmake/meson/make/gcc/clang/ld/python/pip/install/test/runtime)
# phase:         出错阶段 (configuration/compilation/linking/installation/testing/runtime)
# error_signature: 正则表达式(|分隔), 用于精确匹配日志文本
id:                     E227
trigger_tool: git|git diff|pre-commit
phase: validation
error_signature: trailing whitespace\.|new blank line at EOF\.|raw patch line == ' '

# ═══ Layer 1: 识别层 (Recognition) ═══
# severity:      3=🔴blocking  2=🟡medium  1=🟢minor  0=✅resolved
# category:      分类标签 (自由文本, 用于分组过滤)
# match_keywords: 纯文本关键词(逗号分隔), 用于粗筛(固定字符串匹配F)
# title:         简短标题(一句话描述错误模式)
severity: 2
category: unified-diff-context-whitespace
match_keywords: git diff --check, unified diff, patch context, blank-at-eol, single space, fuzz=0
title: Distinguish unified patch context prefixes from source trailing whitespace

# ═══ Layer 2: 诊断层 (Diagnosis) ═══
# root_cause:       一句话根因描述(逗号可分行)
# affected_scope:   影响范围
# verification_cmd: 验证诊断是否正确的命令
root_cause: A canonical unified diff prefixes every unchanged context line with one space; when the unchanged source line is empty, the patch file therefore contains a raw single-space line that an outer repository git diff --check can classify as blank-at-eol even though the patched source has no trailing whitespace.
affected_scope: New or renamed canonical unified patch files audited as ordinary text by an outer Git repository.
verification_cmd: Confirm the source edit has no trailing whitespace, classify each flagged raw single-space line as unified-diff context, then require git apply --check and GNU patch --dry-run --fuzz=0 -p1.

# ═══ Layer 3: 方案层 (Solution Space) ★ ═══
# 推荐方案 (priority 越小越优先, 从 1 开始)
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: split-source-and-patch-whitespace-validation
rec_description: Run git diff --check on non-patch changes and validate patch files with both Git and GNU patch parsers at zero fuzz.
rec_command: git diff <base>...HEAD --check -- . ':(exclude,glob)**/*.patch'; git apply --check <patches>; patch --dry-run --fuzz=0 -p1 -d <source> -i <patch>
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual

# 回退方案 (当推荐方案不可用时尝试)
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach: framework-patch-whitespace-attributes
fallback_description: In a separate framework PR, narrowly configure patch-file whitespace attributes while retaining all non-patch whitespace checks.
fallback_command: *.patch whitespace=-blank-at-eol,-blank-at-eof
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual

# ★ 禁止策略 (与推荐方案同等重要) ★
# forbid_N_pattern:     正则(|分隔), 匹配则拒绝/警告
# forbid_N_reason:      为什么禁止
# forbid_N_consequence: 违反后的后果
forbid_1_pattern: remove.*source.*blank|strip.*context|unified.*n=0|disable.*whitespace
forbid_1_reason: These workarounds either change unrelated source formatting, weaken patch placement evidence, corrupt canonical context, or hide genuine non-patch whitespace defects.
forbid_1_consequence: The patch may become less reviewable or unsafe while real whitespace regressions go undetected.
# forbid_2_pattern:
# forbid_2_reason:
# forbid_2_consequence:

# ═══ Layer 4: 原则引用 ═══
# principles:    适用的原则 ID 列表(逗号分隔), 在 graph/principles.kv 中定义
principles:

# ═══ 关系图 (Relations) ═══
# causes:          本模式是这些模式的根因 (修好本模式可能同时解决它们)
# caused_by:       本模式的根因是这些模式 (应先修它们)
# similar_to:      特征相似可能混淆的模式
# conflicts_with:  解决方案互相冲突的模式
# prerequisite_of: 本模式是修复这些模式的前置条件
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

